{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"The reproduced geometry exposes a concrete overlooked handoff: the tiny agent can pin a main avatar from different sides. A below-pin isolates vertical movement; a side-pin should isolate inward movement. I’m testing that context now, because it determines whether the apparent “one-sided center crossing” reset was caused by the crossing itself or by the first avatar silently leaving its switch."}}
